{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846182-sandbox-enhancing-hacks-for-beast","id":846182,"title":"Sandbox enhancing hacks for Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T10:47:37-08:00","id":846182,"title":"Sandbox enhancing hacks for Beast","content":"Thought I'd share some hacks that I've been developing for my troupe.<br /> <br /> A new (un)Family of Beasts.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Y\u2019tomim: Nightmares Astray</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Her first thought is to wait. Surely someone will realize that she\u2019s been left behind. But long minutes crawl by and loneliness sets in. Maybe, she reasons, she can find her own way home. It is only then that she realizes that she isn\u2019t alone. There\u2019s something there in the dark with her. She can\u2019t see it. It has no form. But it is there nonetheless. Her breath comes raggedly as the need to get away crashes down around her and she runs. How did this place become so maze-like she asks herself as she flies around corner after corner. In the end she gasps in relief thinking that she\u2019s evaded whatever it was only to feel its formless limbs envelop her and drag her kicking and screaming into the darkness around it.</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You\u2019ve always found the overbearing confidence and arrogance of others insufferable. You constantly danced to their tune like a marionette. Now the shoe is on the other foot. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You\u2019ve awoken to a power that you never knew you had within you. You don\u2019t know where it comes from but you\u2019re glad you have it. Now they dance to your music.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You\u2019ve become a cold reminder in the dark recesses of their minds that agency cannot come at the expense of the agency of others. Other people\u2019s dreams are not mere stepping stones to achieving your own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lives</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She has a non-descript house nestled deep in a wooded lot. The shadows grow long and visitors easily lose their way. Sometimes children whisper about the old house and say it\u2019s haunted but mostly people forget that it\u2019s even there. Only in the dark of the night do they remember why they shouldn\u2019t go near such places.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He works in a small cubicle where everyone sees him come and go day after day without really realizing who he is or what he does. His appearance is well kept but nondescript. He lives in a small basement apartment in the middle of a run-down neighborhood but no one ever bothers him because no one ever really remembers that he\u2019s there. For the most part he\u2019s fine with this lot in life but occasionally he\u2019ll see something that makes him want to intervene and set things to rights.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He rolls his eyes when the senior partners brag about their achievements. Their eyes pass right over him like he was just a piece of furniture. They take his empty presence for granted--just another fixture of their day-to-day existence. Every now and again he takes them down a peg from the comfortable setting of their own dreaming minds.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She\u2019s always been a wallflower. A long history of being talked over and ignored has taught her that no one values her input. Even when she adds a valuable point to the conversation people just breeze on past it until someone else brings it up. It doesn\u2019t really bother her though. She knows that she\u2019ll catch up with them soon enough and then they\u2019ll know what it\u2019s like to be trodden down. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stories:</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Y\u2019tomim (singular Yatom) or Orphans are unlike other Beasts in that they don\u2019t represent stories that anyone remembers. Long forgotten, they are more closely related to the multitude of formless things that humanity has yet to encounter and does not know. No human tongue has voiced such tales for if they had, the formless would have been lent a shape and be orphaned no more.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instead Orphans fill the void of represented by humanity\u2019s collective fear of the unknown. It\u2019s fear of change. As such every Y\u2019tomim\u2019s story is merely a beginning. It is a chrysalis for a thing yet to be. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">How the story develops and turns out varies according to the individuals who have roles in it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Horror:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The nightmares of Y\u2019tomim are those of the unknown. They are cloaked in darkness and the dreamer\u2019s antagonist is often formless, invisible, or so deep in shadow that it\u2019s true nature cannot be made out.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Being lost in a claustrophobic environment like an endless maze of tunnels or caves or a never-ending expanse of twisted and overgrown woodland are common nightmare-scapes. The Orphan\u2019s Horror typically lets the dreamer proceed at their own pace, allowing their self-confidence to lead them deeper and deeper into the labyrinth that sprawls around them. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As time goes on the dreamer slowly begins to feel the Horror\u2019s presence and they struggle to escape only to discover that they have been outmaneuvered, outthought, or outfought by the Y\u2019tomim\u2019s canny Horror. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Lair:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Orphans create Lairs that constantly twist in upon themselves. Their landscapes are designed to confound and confuse their prey, leaving their faith in the abilities broken and shattered.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suggested Lair Traits: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cramped, Disruption, Downpour, Echoing, Engulfing, Fog, Maze, Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Undergrowth, Viscous</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Birthright:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Y\u2019tomim have seemingly been disowned by the Dark Mother. Unlike other Beasts they can employ their Kinship abilities on their brethren and sistren. Both parties can realize the full range of benefits that this normally allows.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Because their Horrors are so nebulous in form, Y\u2019tomim can realize additional benefits from teaching lessons to mortals. Anytime an Orphan teaches a mortal a valuable lesson about their limitations while feeding, she gains one additional Satiety beyond those she would normally gain from the feeding. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nickname</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Orphans</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Atavisms</b>:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> None. Y\u2019tomim begin play with only one Atavism.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Adoption</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">An Orphan may be uplifted into one of the known families by finding another Beast who is willing to adopt her. Both parties must join their Lairs together. Thereafter they hold a simple ritual wherein each of them slice open the palms of their hands, share blood, and sacrifice one dot of Willpower.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thereafter, the newly adopted Beast replaces her Birthright with her adoptive parent\u2019s Birthright and gains one of her parent\u2019s In-Family Atavism that is known to her parent.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And some cross-over helpful/sandbox expanding merits:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Castellan (1~5 dots)</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Effect:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> You have a supernatural ally that has taken up residence in one of your Lair\u2019s Chambers. At only one dot, this being is more mortal than supernatural (e.g., it is a Ghoul, Stigmatic, Wolf-Blooded, etc.). At two or more dots the entity is a true supernatural being (e.g., it is a Vampire, Demon, Werewolf, etc.). The Supernatural should be built with 5 additional experiences for each dot of Castellan beyond 2 (i.e., at Castellan 4, the supernatural has 10 experiences). This merit works in all ways like the Retainer merit. At three dots and above, it also works as the Mentor merit at an equivalent rating of Castellan dots - 2. Whatever kind of entity the Castellan is, it gains a limited form of Primordial Pathways which it can use to come and go from its Chamber and is in all ways, your invited guest. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drawbacks:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> For the purposes of calculating Satiety loss due to Time, your Lair trait counts as one higher for every two dots (round up) of this merit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Haunted (1~5 dots)</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> -- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Effect: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your Horror has permitted one or more ephemeral beings to take up residence in one of the Lair\u2019s Chambers. This merit acts as either Retainer or Staff (chosen when it is purchased). In the first case, the ephemeral being\u2019s rank is equal to the dots in this merit. In the second case the dots in this merit represent a like number of Rank 1 ephemeral beings. They cannot leave the Chamber in which they reside. They may be Angels, Ghosts, Spirits, or other ephemeral beings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spawn (1~5 dots)</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Effect:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Your Horror has spawned a multitude of tiny Horrors. Dots of this merit act as dots of Allies or Staff interchangeably. Among other things these Rank 1 ephemeral beings can come and go from the Lair at their leisure and may be used to gather information regarding the surrounding Hive and Primordial Dream. They will also savagely attack any intruders that enter the Lair. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drawbacks: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">You lose additional Satiety equal to the dots of this merit once per month. This loss can be spread across the month.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Steward (1~5 dots)</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Effect:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> You have a mortal servant that you trust to look after affairs within your Lair. This mortal is your invited guest and has taken up residence in your Lair. Dots in this merit act exactly like dots in Retainer except that the mortal also gains a limited form of Primordial Pathways which they can use to come and go from the Lair.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 03-12-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:21:24-08:00","id":846363,"title":"","content":"Well, these are some interesting ideas here. Especially the Orphans. Of course, all that's missing for them are Atavisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T20:50:35-08:00","id":846421,"title":"","content":"Since they have/are no Family they have no in-family atavisms (so by design). Think Revenant in Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:12:47-07:00","id":846529,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. So, are they more like Analysts in that they get another addition in a different set of powers? Analysts focused more on Exploits, so I assume Nightmares might be where the Orphans could specialize in place of having Family Atavisms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:52:19-07:00","id":846540,"title":"","content":"They're more like &quot;No Agenda&quot;. They gain extra Satiety for teaching lessons. Their innate lack of myth and form also let's them mooch off of other Beasts using Family Dinner. So no innate advantages with Nightmares.<br /> <br /> You play an Orphan when you want to play someone who's an outsider among other Beasts. (It fufills a particular player personality with respect to game design.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:06:49-07:00","id":846551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846182-sandbox-enhancing-hacks-for-beast?p=846540#post846540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're more like &quot;No Agenda&quot;. They gain extra Satiety for teaching lessons. Their innate lack of myth and form also let's them mooch off of other Beasts using Family Dinner. So no innate advantages with Nightmares.<br /> <br /> You play an Orphan when you want to play someone who's an outsider among other Beasts. (It fufills a particular player personality with respect to game design.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. And I agree that they do fill a niche among the Begotten. I might tweak them somewhat for my stuff, though, if it's alright.<br /> <br /> Specifically, I'd make them play a wild card role a la Unchained Analysts. I'd also give them an EXP discount for Nightmares to further emphasize their focus on Kinship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-13-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:15:01-07:00","id":846592,"title":"","content":"Have at it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:41:02-07:00","id":846653,"title":"","content":"One more hack I originally meant to post with the others. The exception that makes the rule as it were:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Techgnostic Horror (1 dot)</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> -- </span></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Effect:</span></i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Your Horror is inexplicably more closely linked to the God-Machine than to the Dark Mother. No one knows why this is but you count only Demons and Angels as being </span></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Descended from the Dark Mother</span></i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and </span></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kinship Does Not Apply</span></i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> to Vampires, Werewolves, Prometheans, Changelings, Mummies, etc. </span></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drawbacks:</span></i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> This reversal of the natural order doesn\u2019t sit well with other Beasts who have a Hostile impression when meeting a character with this merit for the first time. </span></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This merit may only be purchased at character creation.</span></i></span></span></i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:10:04-07:00","id":846734,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow. This is quite an interesting reversal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-cate